From 9629961c3a328e37bba61d20b97392803e565eef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:48:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix inflated total counts of UMI-subsampled synthetic
 doublets

subsample_counts thinned the counts of the selected genes first and only
then took original_totals - current_totals as the part of each total that
still had to be subsampled, so the counts just removed from the selected
genes were drawn a second time. The expected total was
rate * T + rate * (1 - rate) * F (T: all-gene total, F: selected-gene
total) instead of rate * T, and the simulated doublets were normalised to
1e6 with the inflated totals. Measure the unselected part before thinning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
